model g6_refusal_order_later_leg
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
  note "T, pre-M1 (#97, chunk 4, P13): which refusal a place keeps when a decision's leg dated after its own day meets a plan's leg on that day (E §4.1, tally 2.1.6's typed movement order, #57): decision sweep on 3 January with its leg on 10 January and plan a on 10 January, both into gone after its lifespan ends (RUN-LIFESPAN), both refused at src; the decision's instance is dated first, so its leg takes its place before the plan's and bal(src) keeps its refusal. Its twin is g6/refusal_order_twin, where one leg refuses alone"

source card "a card"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

input amt: money DUK

input d0: date

input d1: date

place src: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

place gone: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..2025-01-05

move a: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from src to gone amount amt

move sweep: transfers
  on d1
  reads src
  leg cash from src to gone amount min(amt, bal(src)) on d0

ask q: bal(src, 2025-01-31)

version facts
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 1.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  d1 = 2025-01-03
  opening[src] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[gone] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
